WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.486 --> 00:00:29.404
IN THE NEAR FUTURE

2
00:00:29.487 --> 00:00:31.823
THE SEA LEVEL RISES
DUE TO RAPID CLIMATE CHANGE

3
00:00:31.906 --> 00:00:33.825
AND HUMANS DECIDE TO RELOCATE TO SPACE

4
00:00:33.908 --> 00:00:34.868
SPACE

5
00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:38.121
AFTER SUCCESSFULLY BUILDING SHELTERS

6
00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.290
BETWEEN EARTH
AND THE MOON'S ORBITAL PLANES

7
00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:43.209
THEY SPEND DECADES MIGRATING CITIZENS
TO THE 80 OR SO SHELTERS

8
00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:44.294
SHELTERS

9
00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:46.796
AS THE HUMANS SETTLE DOWN...

10
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.173
SHELTERS NO. 8, 12, AND 13

11
00:00:48.256 --> 00:00:50.175
DECLARE THEMSELVES THE ADRIAN REPUBLIC

12
00:00:50.258 --> 00:00:53.511
AND THEY BEGIN ATTACKING EARTH
AND OTHER SHELTERS INDISCRIMINATELY

13
00:00:53.595 --> 00:00:54.596
ADRIAN REPUBLIC

14
00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.390
THIS LEADS TO DECADES OF WAR

15
00:00:57.474 --> 00:01:00.226
BETWEEN THE ALLIED FORCE
AND THE ADRIAN REPUBLIC

16
00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:01.144
WAR

17
00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:05.565
HUMANS LEFT ON EARTH CONTINUE
TO PRODUCE MUNITIONS

18
00:01:05.648 --> 00:01:07.859
LIVING LIKE COGS
IN THE MACHINE THAT IS WAR

19
00:01:07.942 --> 00:01:09.152
HUMANS

20
00:02:58.428 --> 00:03:01.681
<i>- Team 45, do you copy?</i>
- It's Captain Yun Jung-yi.

21
00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:05.476
<i>Captain Yun, there was a nearby explosion.
Are you still alive?</i>

22
00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.729
How else would I answer you? Jeez.

23
00:03:08.438 --> 00:03:11.024
<i>What's your team's status?
Did you reach the fuel rod?</i>

24
00:03:11.649 --> 00:03:12.817
We're here,

25
00:03:15.153 --> 00:03:16.321
but it's looking bleak.

26
00:03:23.119 --> 00:03:24.245
What is that?

27
00:03:24.329 --> 00:03:27.123
<i>We were informed
that Adrian's new ZIMBO is there.</i>

28
00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:29.167
Damn, thanks for telling me so early.

29
00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.711
<i>This ZIMBO's energy battery
is in the rear.</i>

30
00:03:31.794 --> 00:03:33.796
<i>Target that. Target the rear!</i>

31
00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.375
<i>Backup will arrive soon.</i>

32
00:04:11.209 --> 00:04:12.710
As if I can wait...

33
00:07:11.472 --> 00:07:12.807
I already checked that.

34
00:07:13.307 --> 00:07:14.809
I told you to set it up right.

35
00:07:15.893 --> 00:07:17.186
- Check the rail gun.
- Roger.

36
00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:22.358
Man, she failed to escape
at the exact same point.

37
00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:23.276
I know.

38
00:07:24.402 --> 00:07:26.779
I'll send for a detailed lab analysis.

39
00:07:26.863 --> 00:07:28.072
Yes, do that now.

40
00:07:28.698 --> 00:07:29.532
Oh, you're here.

41
00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:34.954
Man, what on earth is the problem?

42
00:07:35.037 --> 00:07:38.082
But she sure is a legendary mercenary.

43
00:07:38.666 --> 00:07:41.794
Look at how many robots she destroyed
getting to this point.

44
00:07:41.878 --> 00:07:42.712
I know.

45
00:07:43.212 --> 00:07:45.840
Maybe the enemy's programming
is poorly done.

46
00:07:46.507 --> 00:07:49.343
I think we should start
with a different setup tomorrow.

47
00:07:49.427 --> 00:07:50.970
Oh, no.

48
00:07:51.053 --> 00:07:53.097
Hey, we can't tamper with that.

49
00:07:53.181 --> 00:07:57.101
We must replicate the real circumstances
to better understand her brain map.

50
00:07:57.977 --> 00:08:01.564
Wrap up for today.
We have important guests coming.

51
00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:03.191
- Yes, Chief.
- Yes, ma'am.

52
00:08:15.953 --> 00:08:16.913
- Here.
- Yes.

53
00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:26.964
Let's get moving.

54
00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:50.029
- Should I send this to Tech Support?
- Yes, that's right.

55
00:09:15.096 --> 00:09:17.098
We'll finish things up before we go.

56
00:09:17.181 --> 00:09:18.015
Okay.

57
00:10:26.584 --> 00:10:27.585
Hold on.

58
00:10:28.252 --> 00:10:29.086
This.

59
00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:30.755
You sure this is fresh?

60
00:10:32.256 --> 00:10:33.758
We just caught it.

61
00:10:35.176 --> 00:10:36.135
I mean...

62
00:10:37.345 --> 00:10:39.555
it has an awfully resentful expression.

63
00:10:42.642 --> 00:10:44.060
Don't get all tensed up.

64
00:10:45.227 --> 00:10:47.229
It's a joke. A joke.

65
00:10:49.899 --> 00:10:50.858
I'm counting on you.

66
00:10:55.988 --> 00:10:57.698
Okay, let's pick up the pace.

67
00:10:58.282 --> 00:11:00.409
You know today is really important, right?

68
00:11:11.671 --> 00:11:13.673
Oh, Chief, you're here.

69
00:11:14.674 --> 00:11:16.550
Thank you for your hard work.

70
00:11:16.634 --> 00:11:17.760
Director.

71
00:11:18.886 --> 00:11:20.930
Is all this really necessary?

72
00:11:21.472 --> 00:11:22.932
They're all elders.

73
00:11:23.015 --> 00:11:26.018
Older people consider these things
more important than you'd think.

74
00:11:29.063 --> 00:11:31.190
You aren't nervous, are you?

75
00:11:31.857 --> 00:11:33.317
Slept well last night?

76
00:11:34.402 --> 00:11:35.236
Yes.

77
00:11:36.779 --> 00:11:38.364
Are you feeling okay, sir?

78
00:11:38.447 --> 00:11:40.074
You look very nervous.

79
00:11:40.157 --> 00:11:42.201
What... me?

80
00:11:45.705 --> 00:11:47.873
Presentations require showmanship.

81
00:11:47.957 --> 00:11:50.126
I'm focused on that. That's why.

82
00:11:51.001 --> 00:11:54.171
Stiffly reading off a script
isn't a presentation.

83
00:11:55.047 --> 00:11:57.967
You need to be humorous like me,

84
00:11:58.968 --> 00:12:02.722
while serving great food and cocktails.

85
00:12:03.639 --> 00:12:06.100
That's how we get unstinting support
for the company.

86
00:12:07.059 --> 00:12:08.144
You get it, right?

87
00:12:19.655 --> 00:12:21.490
Greetings, I'm Kra... ro...

88
00:12:25.536 --> 00:12:29.123
Greetings, I'm Kronoid's... Lab Director,

89
00:12:29.623 --> 00:12:30.708
Kim Sang-hoon.

90
00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:35.504
Shall we start?

91
00:12:48.642 --> 00:12:50.644
{\an8}<i>Year 2135.</i>

92
00:12:51.312 --> 00:12:53.689
{\an8}<i>The rising sea level
and depletion of resources</i>

93
00:12:53.773 --> 00:12:57.943
{\an8}<i>led mankind
to look for new ways to survive.</i>

94
00:13:00.112 --> 00:13:02.990
{\an8}<i>And we found new opportunities</i>

95
00:13:03.073 --> 00:13:05.075
{\an8}<i>in the shelters built in space.</i>

96
00:13:05.993 --> 00:13:07.495
{\an8}<i>But shortly after,</i>

97
00:13:07.578 --> 00:13:11.290
{\an8}<i>Space Shelters no. 8, 12, and 13</i>

98
00:13:11.999 --> 00:13:15.085
{\an8}<i>declared themselves the Adrian Republic,</i>

99
00:13:15.586 --> 00:13:17.713
{\an8}<i>starting a civil war, threatening Earth</i>

100
00:13:17.797 --> 00:13:19.673
{\an8}<i>and the rest of the shelters.</i>

101
00:13:19.757 --> 00:13:21.634
I narrated this myself.

102
00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:28.057
{\an8}<i>This war between the Allied Force
and the Adrian Republic</i>

103
00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:30.684
{\an8}<i>has been ongoing for the last 40 years.</i>

104
00:13:31.894 --> 00:13:34.480
I also directed the music and everything.

105
00:13:35.773 --> 00:13:37.650
<i>The AI-developing Kronoid Lab</i>

106
00:13:37.733 --> 00:13:40.528
<i>was founded in the year 2130 CE,</i>

107
00:13:40.611 --> 00:13:42.738
<i>with top-notch researchers
and cutting-edge...</i>

108
00:13:42.822 --> 00:13:45.741
We all know this. Skip to the point.

109
00:13:46.242 --> 00:13:47.076
Oh...

110
00:13:47.785 --> 00:13:49.286
Hey, fast-forward!

111
00:13:54.291 --> 00:13:57.586
<i>Adrian Civil War's legendary mercenary,
the pride of Korea,</i>

112
00:13:58.212 --> 00:13:59.672
<i>she's Captain Yun Jung-yi.</i>

113
00:14:00.214 --> 00:14:05.177
{\an8}<i>The leader of Squadron 8 Team 45,
Captain Yun Jung-yi</i>

114
00:14:05.261 --> 00:14:07.847
<i>partook in countless missions</i>

115
00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:10.099
<i>and achieved great results.</i>

116
00:14:11.433 --> 00:14:13.435
Shall we skip over the stuff we know?

117
00:14:16.689 --> 00:14:18.482
<i>Thirty-five years ago, Captain Yun</i>

118
00:14:19.149 --> 00:14:23.320
<i>joined the bombing operation
of a fuel rod in Adrian's Shelter B-25,</i>

119
00:14:23.988 --> 00:14:27.825
<i>but the mission was a failure,
and she ended up in a coma.</i>

120
00:14:28.909 --> 00:14:31.662
<i>With permission from her bereaved family,</i>

121
00:14:32.246 --> 00:14:35.666
<i>Kronoid has spared nothing
for her recovery,</i>

122
00:14:35.749 --> 00:14:38.335
<i>copying her brain
and converting it into data.</i>

123
00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:42.923
<i>With all her tactical knowledge,
combat skills,</i>

124
00:14:43.007 --> 00:14:45.968
<i>as well as her strong loyalty
and determination,</i>

125
00:14:46.051 --> 00:14:49.388
<i>we will develop
the greatest AI to command combat.</i>

126
00:14:49.471 --> 00:14:50.306
Right.

127
00:14:51.515 --> 00:14:53.142
We plan to name this

128
00:14:53.225 --> 00:14:54.768
the "JUNG_E" program.

129
00:14:55.728 --> 00:14:58.981
This was created
so Captain Yun's spirit would live on.

130
00:15:02.318 --> 00:15:03.694
Oh, and Captain Yun's...

131
00:15:04.236 --> 00:15:06.071
Her daughter, Dr. Yun Seo-hyun,

132
00:15:06.155 --> 00:15:08.741
plans to finalize the project
as the team lead.

133
00:15:09.950 --> 00:15:12.244
Shall we discuss this further with her?

134
00:15:12.995 --> 00:15:13.829
Chief!

135
00:15:15.414 --> 00:15:16.749
Don't be nervous, okay?

136
00:15:32.222 --> 00:15:35.601
This is the replicated data
from Ms. Yun's brain.

137
00:15:37.019 --> 00:15:38.228
We are developing an AI

138
00:15:38.729 --> 00:15:41.815
that focuses on reflecting
her combat skills and experience,

139
00:15:41.899 --> 00:15:44.902
based on her replicated brain data

140
00:15:45.527 --> 00:15:47.947
from her final mission.

141
00:15:53.494 --> 00:15:54.411
Just like now,

142
00:15:54.912 --> 00:15:57.957
whenever the android uploaded
with her brain data does something,

143
00:15:58.457 --> 00:16:01.502
her behavioral pattern
is marked like this.

144
00:16:05.214 --> 00:16:06.298
This part here

145
00:16:07.299 --> 00:16:10.594
shows the strongest reaction
when in combat.

146
00:16:12.221 --> 00:16:15.432
Shall we mark that part in green?

147
00:16:16.392 --> 00:16:19.019
Since our projects are always green-lit.

148
00:16:19.103 --> 00:16:20.020
Ding, ding!

149
00:16:20.854 --> 00:16:21.689
Having fun?

150
00:16:23.607 --> 00:16:25.067
It was a joke.

151
00:16:26.402 --> 00:16:29.571
We're going to use these simulations
to extract and develop

152
00:16:30.239 --> 00:16:32.700
only the combat-related data
from Ms. Yun's brain data,

153
00:16:33.742 --> 00:16:38.122
and create the greatest combat AI.

154
00:16:38.789 --> 00:16:39.623
So,

155
00:16:40.666 --> 00:16:42.918
did the robot manage to escape?

156
00:16:45.421 --> 00:16:46.588
Not yet.

157
00:16:46.672 --> 00:16:48.090
All of this sounds good,

158
00:16:49.091 --> 00:16:51.510
but if she had succeeded
in the final mission,

159
00:16:51.593 --> 00:16:53.387
the war would already be over.

160
00:16:54.346 --> 00:16:56.682
That failure is why the Adrian Civil War

161
00:16:56.765 --> 00:16:58.642
is still ongoing after 40 years.

162
00:16:59.768 --> 00:17:01.353
The Korean mercenary...

163
00:17:02.438 --> 00:17:03.772
She was popular back then.

164
00:17:04.857 --> 00:17:06.400
But now, many people think

165
00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:11.780
that Yun Jung-yi is the reason
the war has been dragging on.

166
00:17:11.864 --> 00:17:14.742
Oh, what a heated debate!

167
00:17:16.035 --> 00:17:17.911
But our combat AI is different.

168
00:17:18.662 --> 00:17:21.040
We're making every effort
to extract only her

169
00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:23.208
combatting strengths...

170
00:17:23.709 --> 00:17:27.296
Then why does it keep failing
to escape from the same simulation?

171
00:17:28.881 --> 00:17:31.592
Why would you develop a combat AI

172
00:17:32.551 --> 00:17:35.345
using the brain of a soldier
who failed her mission?

173
00:17:35.429 --> 00:17:36.263
She...

174
00:17:38.307 --> 00:17:39.141
will escape.

175
00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:41.435
We will make sure

176
00:17:41.518 --> 00:17:45.647
Capt. Yun Jung-yi escapes that simulation.

177
00:17:45.731 --> 00:17:46.565
Plus,

178
00:17:47.191 --> 00:17:51.528
we'll make her a lasting hero
of the Allied Force.

179
00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:29.900
That's by a famous artist.
It's the Yun Jung-yi edition.

180
00:18:30.567 --> 00:18:31.401
Great, huh?

181
00:18:32.903 --> 00:18:34.613
The sunset looks great, too.

182
00:18:39.159 --> 00:18:40.369
Wow, it arrived already.

183
00:18:42.079 --> 00:18:42.913
Adorable, no?

184
00:18:44.915 --> 00:18:47.126
I heard people in the old days

185
00:18:47.626 --> 00:18:51.046
focused on a product's design
over its practicality.

186
00:18:52.172 --> 00:18:54.341
Sure, everything was abundant back then.

187
00:18:55.551 --> 00:18:56.385
Right.

188
00:18:57.344 --> 00:18:59.012
Your vehemence at the end!

189
00:19:00.973 --> 00:19:02.766
It moved me, really!

190
00:19:04.184 --> 00:19:05.686
Those old fogies went silent.

191
00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:09.189
They secretly told me
that we can start supplying

192
00:19:10.566 --> 00:19:13.902
once the AI passes the simulation test.

193
00:19:15.070 --> 00:19:15.946
That's good.

194
00:19:17.531 --> 00:19:18.365
Take a seat.

195
00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:23.912
Would you like coffee?
The taste of the 20th century.

196
00:19:24.538 --> 00:19:25.372
No, thank you.

197
00:19:26.248 --> 00:19:29.001
I have to interview number 17
before termination.

198
00:19:29.585 --> 00:19:30.502
Oh, the interview.

199
00:19:32.045 --> 00:19:34.381
Do we really need to do that
before terminations?

200
00:19:34.882 --> 00:19:35.716
Chief.

201
00:19:36.633 --> 00:19:38.886
Does it help with understanding
the brain map?

202
00:19:40.387 --> 00:19:44.641
Well, the more accurately
we understand it, the better.

203
00:19:51.523 --> 00:19:52.524
You're happy, right?

204
00:19:52.608 --> 00:19:56.195
The company's signature product,
which just might end this war,

205
00:19:56.278 --> 00:19:59.072
being launched in your mother's name.

206
00:20:01.533 --> 00:20:02.910
All thanks to the chairman.

207
00:20:09.917 --> 00:20:12.002
The chairman is a great man.

208
00:20:13.962 --> 00:20:16.006
You've known him longer than I have.

209
00:20:16.757 --> 00:20:18.258
I've only worked for him

210
00:20:18.342 --> 00:20:20.177
for a little over ten years.

211
00:20:20.969 --> 00:20:24.097
You met him when you were young
because of your mother.

212
00:20:25.724 --> 00:20:28.477
It's more like he's taken care of me
since I was young.

213
00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:31.355
Now that the "JUNG_E" project is back on,

214
00:20:31.939 --> 00:20:33.899
forget about what that old fart said.

215
00:20:35.484 --> 00:20:36.610
Captain Yun was

216
00:20:37.361 --> 00:20:39.738
a globally popular soldier.

217
00:20:40.697 --> 00:20:42.908
And yet, he picks on one measly failure.

218
00:20:45.369 --> 00:20:47.704
She's popular, that's why. He's jealous.

219
00:20:49.164 --> 00:20:50.916
Your mother's still alive,

220
00:20:50.999 --> 00:20:53.168
all thanks to our chairman.

221
00:20:53.252 --> 00:20:56.213
Also, he seems to have high hopes
for this project.

222
00:20:56.296 --> 00:20:57.965
I really, truly, really...

223
00:21:00.217 --> 00:21:01.802
I'm counting on you, Chief.

224
00:21:03.845 --> 00:21:04.805
Don't worry.

225
00:21:06.348 --> 00:21:10.018
It's time for the interview.
I'll have to excuse myself.

226
00:21:10.102 --> 00:21:11.311
Oh, yes, of course.

227
00:21:13.146 --> 00:21:14.982
The chairman will be visiting soon,

228
00:21:15.607 --> 00:21:17.818
so let's keep up the good work!

229
00:21:52.936 --> 00:21:54.146
ACTIVATE

230
00:21:57.274 --> 00:21:58.525
Hello, Ms. Yun?

231
00:21:59.860 --> 00:22:02.070
Ms. Yun, pull yourself together.

232
00:22:02.904 --> 00:22:04.364
Ms. Yun, can you hear me?

233
00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:06.325
Is the mic on?

234
00:22:06.408 --> 00:22:08.493
I think she can hear me fine. Ms. Yun!

235
00:22:20.714 --> 00:22:21.548
Uh...

236
00:22:25.052 --> 00:22:27.220
BRAIN MAP SENSORY CONTROL
PAIN LEVEL DECREASING

237
00:22:29.556 --> 00:22:32.851
Okay, how's that?
The pain is bearable now, right?

238
00:22:33.518 --> 00:22:35.062
Now let's calm down and talk...

239
00:22:35.145 --> 00:22:38.357
What's this? I can't feel my body.

240
00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:40.359
Come on, try to calm down...

241
00:22:41.234 --> 00:22:43.987
Where am I?

242
00:22:44.071 --> 00:22:45.989
Who are you? Did you do this to me?

243
00:22:46.073 --> 00:22:47.115
Let me go!

244
00:22:49.368 --> 00:22:52.537
What the hell have you done to me,
you bastards?

245
00:22:54.122 --> 00:22:55.499
I can't get through to her.

246
00:22:58.251 --> 00:23:00.754
I'm going to kill all of you bastards!

247
00:23:08.595 --> 00:23:10.514
Interview over. Terminate number 17.

248
00:23:59.938 --> 00:24:02.858
It seems like such a waste
to discard them every time.

249
00:24:03.817 --> 00:24:06.611
You did well,
considering it's your first time.

250
00:24:07.237 --> 00:24:09.573
Oh, well, I didn't really do much.

251
00:24:17.789 --> 00:24:21.001
I heard you wanted to transfer
to our team from HQ.

252
00:24:21.084 --> 00:24:21.918
Oh, yes.

253
00:24:22.419 --> 00:24:25.005
I'm actually a fan of Captain Yun.

254
00:24:25.839 --> 00:24:28.425
She was more popular than superheroes
when I was young.

255
00:24:30.177 --> 00:24:31.011
Superheroes?

256
00:24:32.762 --> 00:24:35.474
My mother actually
kept fighting in the war

257
00:24:36.224 --> 00:24:37.642
because of me.

258
00:24:38.643 --> 00:24:39.478
Sorry?

259
00:24:41.271 --> 00:24:42.147
When I was young,

260
00:24:43.607 --> 00:24:45.317
I had a tumor in my lungs.

261
00:24:47.444 --> 00:24:49.196
The treatment cost a fortune.

262
00:24:51.406 --> 00:24:52.240
The only way...

263
00:24:54.326 --> 00:24:58.747
my mother could make that much money
was to become a mercenary.

264
00:25:00.582 --> 00:25:04.711
I always worried
my mother might die because of me,

265
00:25:06.755 --> 00:25:11.134
and I lived in fear
as I watched her head into battles.

266
00:25:13.720 --> 00:25:15.263
The day I got the surgery

267
00:25:17.140 --> 00:25:19.434
was the last day she went to fight.

268
00:25:21.144 --> 00:25:22.521
I always wondered...

269
00:25:24.898 --> 00:25:28.610
"Mom never got to live her life
because of me."

270
00:25:29.486 --> 00:25:31.696
"Did she ever resent me?"

271
00:25:34.282 --> 00:25:35.408
Then why not ask her?

272
00:25:37.327 --> 00:25:38.161
Sorry?

273
00:25:39.079 --> 00:25:41.039
You can ask those things.

274
00:25:41.122 --> 00:25:43.792
When you're done with a test,
ask one in an interview.

275
00:25:43.875 --> 00:25:45.627
If it ever resented its daughter.

276
00:25:46.503 --> 00:25:47.337
Sure.

277
00:25:48.880 --> 00:25:50.549
- I could do that.
- Right.

278
00:25:53.093 --> 00:25:56.471
Anyway, I have the ethics test today.

279
00:25:56.972 --> 00:25:59.891
Jae-kyung, please finish up
no. 17's interview report.

280
00:25:59.975 --> 00:26:02.936
Oh, the ethics test... Yes, ma'am.

281
00:26:07.732 --> 00:26:10.193
Uh, ma'am. Thank you for the story.

282
00:26:10.735 --> 00:26:15.073
I'm such a big fan of Yun Jung-yi.
Even those backstories are fun.

283
00:27:08.418 --> 00:27:09.336
Here you go.

284
00:27:09.419 --> 00:27:11.212
Thank you.

285
00:27:11.921 --> 00:27:13.214
Oh, you came again.

286
00:27:41.284 --> 00:27:43.620
Mom, you'll come soon, right?

287
00:27:44.788 --> 00:27:45.622
Of course,

288
00:27:46.247 --> 00:27:49.084
be a good girl when you get there, okay?

289
00:27:52.337 --> 00:27:54.005
Don't cry, it's nothing.

290
00:27:54.923 --> 00:27:57.258
Alright? Don't cry.

291
00:27:58.426 --> 00:28:01.930
It's not like you won't see me again.
Okay?

292
00:28:08.186 --> 00:28:09.020
Seo-hyun.

293
00:28:09.813 --> 00:28:12.482
I have to go on another mission.

294
00:28:13.316 --> 00:28:16.111
So, Mommy can't be with you
when you have the surgery.

295
00:28:17.821 --> 00:28:19.656
But you'll be okay without me, right?

296
00:28:19.739 --> 00:28:21.825
My daughter is a brave girl, right?

297
00:28:25.578 --> 00:28:26.413
Mom.

298
00:28:28.164 --> 00:28:29.332
And when I'm done?

299
00:28:30.542 --> 00:28:32.377
Will you be there after the surgery?

300
00:28:33.336 --> 00:28:34.462
Of course.

301
00:28:35.046 --> 00:28:38.508
I'm planning to finish this mission
real quick.

302
00:28:39.259 --> 00:28:43.513
I'll be right by your side
after your surgery, okay?

303
00:28:47.475 --> 00:28:49.144
Honey, give me a lucky cheek rub.

304
00:28:51.062 --> 00:28:52.105
Come here.

305
00:28:52.188 --> 00:28:53.148
Ah, there's my girl.

306
00:28:55.483 --> 00:28:56.985
Rub!

307
00:29:11.583 --> 00:29:12.751
She'll be going in now.

308
00:29:21.593 --> 00:29:24.095
I'll see you soon. You can do it. Okay?

309
00:29:51.915 --> 00:29:56.669
<i>This is the eighth ethics test
of Kronoid Lab's Chief Yun Seo-hyun.</i>

310
00:29:57.629 --> 00:30:00.799
<i>Ms. Yun, have you ever had a pet?</i>

311
00:30:01.925 --> 00:30:02.884
No.

312
00:30:02.967 --> 00:30:06.221
<i>Have you ever felt attached to a product
or an object?</i>

313
00:30:07.305 --> 00:30:08.139
Yes.

314
00:30:08.223 --> 00:30:10.725
<i>Have you ever named the object?</i>

315
00:30:10.809 --> 00:30:11.643
Yes.

316
00:30:11.726 --> 00:30:15.396
<i>Have you ever written three or more lines
of poetry while watching the sunset?</i>

317
00:30:16.272 --> 00:30:17.106
Yes.

318
00:30:17.607 --> 00:30:19.150
<i>Have you ever bought</i>

319
00:30:19.234 --> 00:30:22.028
<i>an original piece of artwork at a price</i>

320
00:30:22.111 --> 00:30:24.197
<i>that feels too expensive for your means?</i>

321
00:30:24.823 --> 00:30:25.657
No.

322
00:30:26.282 --> 00:30:29.410
The test results will be sent
to the company in two to three days.

323
00:30:30.954 --> 00:30:32.622
But above all, the scan results show

324
00:30:32.705 --> 00:30:36.167
that the cancer cells are spreading
from your previous surgery area.

325
00:30:36.251 --> 00:30:39.087
Ms. Yun, as I've told you before,

326
00:30:39.170 --> 00:30:43.800
cancer has spread past your lungs
to all your other organs.

327
00:30:44.384 --> 00:30:46.219
Surgery is impossible at this point.

328
00:30:48.346 --> 00:30:49.514
If this was inevitable,

329
00:30:51.516 --> 00:30:53.518
I guess the surgery was all for nothing.

330
00:30:53.601 --> 00:30:54.435
Pardon?

331
00:30:55.728 --> 00:30:56.563
It's nothing.

332
00:30:57.647 --> 00:30:58.481
So...

333
00:31:00.149 --> 00:31:01.568
how long do I have left?

334
00:31:02.485 --> 00:31:03.695
Three months at most.

335
00:31:05.530 --> 00:31:09.117
All we can suggest right now
is that you copy your brain,

336
00:31:09.200 --> 00:31:11.160
and switch over to a prosthetic body.

337
00:31:11.995 --> 00:31:15.373
These days, the law guarantees
equal human rights

338
00:31:15.456 --> 00:31:19.085
to those who copy their brains
and switch to prosthetic bodies.

339
00:31:19.168 --> 00:31:21.337
Of course, the price might be an issue...

340
00:31:22.046 --> 00:31:22.881
What if...

341
00:31:24.549 --> 00:31:25.466
I can't afford it?

342
00:31:26.050 --> 00:31:29.387
If Type A is beyond your means,
where you switch to a prosthetic body

343
00:31:29.470 --> 00:31:32.849
using a brain replication system
with guaranteed equal human rights,

344
00:31:34.267 --> 00:31:37.478
I recommend type B,
which limits basic human rights

345
00:31:37.562 --> 00:31:39.480
such as marriage, residential mobility,

346
00:31:39.564 --> 00:31:40.982
and child adoption.

347
00:31:41.608 --> 00:31:45.528
Also, you'll have to consent
to provide your brain data

348
00:31:45.612 --> 00:31:46.779
to government agencies.

349
00:31:47.739 --> 00:31:51.659
If you still find that to be costly,
there is Type C...

350
00:31:52.243 --> 00:31:55.538
You don't get treated as a human being
with Type C.

351
00:31:55.622 --> 00:31:57.790
Well, it's not as bad as you think.

352
00:31:57.874 --> 00:31:59.584
But your brain data

353
00:31:59.667 --> 00:32:03.922
will be provided to certified companies
or those that purchase it,

354
00:32:04.005 --> 00:32:07.216
and they will be making
countless clones with it,

355
00:32:07.300 --> 00:32:10.386
so you won't be recognized
as your own person. No.

356
00:32:11.679 --> 00:32:12.805
But as you know,

357
00:32:13.389 --> 00:32:16.809
Type C costs nothing at all.

358
00:32:17.727 --> 00:32:19.938
Rather, a subsidy is provided
to the bereaved.

359
00:32:20.521 --> 00:32:22.190
Your mother, Captain Yun Jung-yi,

360
00:32:22.815 --> 00:32:25.526
was also contracted
for Type C with Kronoid.

361
00:32:26.861 --> 00:32:27.987
I'll think about it.

362
00:32:29.447 --> 00:32:32.533
Seeing as I'm already here,
I'd like to see my mother.

363
00:32:32.617 --> 00:32:34.285
Sure, okay then.

364
00:32:34.369 --> 00:32:36.579
Give me a call
after you've thought about it.

365
00:32:37.205 --> 00:32:38.039
All right.

366
00:33:08.778 --> 00:33:12.490
Ms. Yun barely survived,
but she is currently unconscious.

367
00:33:13.241 --> 00:33:17.286
If you consent to Type C brain replication
before her cerebral cortex is damaged,

368
00:33:19.789 --> 00:33:21.165
we can avoid brain death.

369
00:33:27.213 --> 00:33:30.800
If you sign the agreement now,
we'll take care of Ms. Yun's treatment,

370
00:33:30.883 --> 00:33:34.554
and her daughter's education fees
and living expenses.

371
00:33:36.764 --> 00:33:39.350
Please read it carefully before you sign.

372
00:33:49.360 --> 00:33:50.862
Poor thing...

373
00:33:50.945 --> 00:33:52.405
Ms. Yun's brain data will be

374
00:33:52.488 --> 00:33:54.991
developed into a product
that will end this tedious war.

375
00:33:56.200 --> 00:33:59.162
We'll relay your decision to the company
and proceed accordingly.

376
00:34:00.121 --> 00:34:02.623
The living expenses will be sent shortly...

377
00:34:04.417 --> 00:34:05.251
Hi Seo-hyun.

378
00:34:10.006 --> 00:34:14.093
I brought a present for you.

379
00:34:20.224 --> 00:34:23.394
Your mom will become an eternal hero.

380
00:34:24.645 --> 00:34:25.855
You'd like that, right?

381
00:35:15.113 --> 00:35:18.491
COPYING BRAIN REPLICATION DATA

382
00:36:00.324 --> 00:36:01.242
NO. 18 READY

383
00:36:01.325 --> 00:36:02.410
No. 18 is good to go.

384
00:36:05.913 --> 00:36:06.831
Do we have access?

385
00:36:07.373 --> 00:36:08.875
Yes, we have a good signal.

386
00:36:23.181 --> 00:36:24.348
No. 18 is in place.

387
00:36:24.849 --> 00:36:26.225
- Min-jae.
- Yes, ma'am.

388
00:36:26.309 --> 00:36:28.352
Check on Labs A, B, and C.

389
00:36:28.436 --> 00:36:29.270
Yes, ma'am.

390
00:36:48.581 --> 00:36:50.374
All figures look good.

391
00:36:52.919 --> 00:36:54.253
Docking complete.

392
00:36:54.837 --> 00:36:55.838
Okay.

393
00:36:55.922 --> 00:36:57.298
I'll prepare the test.

394
00:37:00.426 --> 00:37:01.886
Wait.

395
00:37:04.722 --> 00:37:06.641
Let's start a little differently today.

396
00:37:08.684 --> 00:37:10.186
Let's shoot its leg.

397
00:37:17.902 --> 00:37:18.903
Hurry. Come on.

398
00:37:27.411 --> 00:37:29.038
RAIL GUN CONTROLS
FIRE

399
00:37:33.584 --> 00:37:37.046
The research isn't going anywhere
because we repeat the same simulation.

400
00:37:37.546 --> 00:37:40.967
Now, I'd appreciate it if you could begin.

401
00:38:04.323 --> 00:38:07.702
PAIN LEVEL INCREASING

402
00:38:09.370 --> 00:38:11.664
It's the area that reacted
when no. 17 was shot.

403
00:38:12.540 --> 00:38:14.000
It definitely reacts to pain.

404
00:38:15.543 --> 00:38:17.837
Mark that in red...

405
00:38:18.421 --> 00:38:19.422
Like a traffic light.

406
00:38:21.632 --> 00:38:23.384
It's a joke. A joke.

407
00:38:24.176 --> 00:38:26.012
Traffic light, my ass.

408
00:38:26.971 --> 00:38:29.724
PAIN LEVEL INCREASING

409
00:38:54.665 --> 00:38:55.666
Green light.

410
00:38:56.751 --> 00:38:57.835
Let's go.

411
00:39:16.771 --> 00:39:20.107
WILL TO FIGHT DECREASING
PAIN LEVEL INCREASING

412
00:39:20.691 --> 00:39:24.737
Her will to fight is faltering.
The simulation will end soon.

413
00:39:26.822 --> 00:39:29.367
Ugh, how boring.

414
00:39:39.543 --> 00:39:40.378
Huh? Wait.

415
00:39:42.755 --> 00:39:44.048
UNIDENTIFIED AREA INCREASING

416
00:39:51.514 --> 00:39:52.390
Huh? What's that?

417
00:39:54.350 --> 00:39:56.143
- Which area lit up?
- I'll check.

418
00:39:59.271 --> 00:40:01.982
Its mobility is higher
than the green brainwave signal.

419
00:40:02.691 --> 00:40:03.901
It's an unfamiliar area.

420
00:40:20.793 --> 00:40:21.794
Hey, no!

421
00:40:23.295 --> 00:40:24.755
You can't shoot the head.

422
00:40:24.839 --> 00:40:26.215
Damn it.

423
00:40:28.426 --> 00:40:30.636
- Go in and retrieve it now!
- Yes, sir.

424
00:40:30.719 --> 00:40:32.179
- Replay the scene.
- Yes, sir.

425
00:40:34.056 --> 00:40:36.350
Hey, which part was it?

426
00:40:37.476 --> 00:40:38.394
I'll check.

427
00:40:39.145 --> 00:40:40.729
UNIDENTIFIED AREA INCREASING

428
00:40:41.313 --> 00:40:43.065
This hasn't been activated before.

429
00:40:43.566 --> 00:40:44.942
Oh, what could that be?

430
00:40:46.902 --> 00:40:50.573
From what I see,
that's the key to building combat AIs.

431
00:40:52.283 --> 00:40:55.202
Mark that area in... in yellow.

432
00:40:55.786 --> 00:40:56.704
Answer me!

433
00:40:58.539 --> 00:40:59.373
Yes, sir.

434
00:41:00.749 --> 00:41:04.003
UNIDENTIFIED AREA INCREASING

435
00:41:05.629 --> 00:41:07.298
Okay.

436
00:41:07.381 --> 00:41:10.468
Let's put in some more effort.
We're briefing at HQ tomorrow.

437
00:41:59.099 --> 00:42:02.937
Kronoid... Kronoid's Lab Director.

438
00:42:03.812 --> 00:42:06.941
Hello, I'm Kronoid's Lab Director,
Kim Sang-hoon.

439
00:42:51.235 --> 00:42:52.486
Has the chairman arrived?

440
00:42:53.070 --> 00:42:53.904
I'll check.

441
00:43:03.581 --> 00:43:05.082
The chairman isn't coming today.

442
00:43:07.126 --> 00:43:08.836
Hello, Director Kim.

443
00:43:12.464 --> 00:43:13.424
We haven't met.

444
00:43:14.049 --> 00:43:17.803
I'm Managing Director Lee Se-yeon,
newly joining product development.

445
00:43:22.057 --> 00:43:22.933
Okay.

446
00:43:24.101 --> 00:43:25.603
The chairman isn't coming today?

447
00:43:25.686 --> 00:43:28.355
He's being debriefed on our results.
I'm sure he's coming.

448
00:43:28.939 --> 00:43:30.691
The chairman told me

449
00:43:30.774 --> 00:43:33.944
to attend the presentation on his behalf
and relay it to him.

450
00:43:34.028 --> 00:43:34.903
He told you that?

451
00:43:40.034 --> 00:43:41.535
You're with product development?

452
00:43:41.619 --> 00:43:43.954
I'm Managing Director Lee Se-yeon.

453
00:43:44.038 --> 00:43:45.789
I've just been appointed to...

454
00:43:48.292 --> 00:43:50.336
Anybody heard of product development?

455
00:43:53.547 --> 00:43:55.633
Kronoid is a military AI development firm.

456
00:43:55.716 --> 00:43:57.343
What is meant by product development?

457
00:44:05.601 --> 00:44:06.435
How fun.

458
00:44:07.686 --> 00:44:10.189
Can't hide feelings, just like him!

459
00:44:14.777 --> 00:44:15.819
What?

460
00:44:15.903 --> 00:44:19.114
Anyway, the chairman can't come today

461
00:44:19.198 --> 00:44:21.617
due to a prior engagement.

462
00:44:21.700 --> 00:44:23.077
So I'll be debriefed instead.

463
00:44:23.661 --> 00:44:26.455
The chairman will visit the lab soon,

464
00:44:26.538 --> 00:44:29.041
so you can take easy today, okay?

465
00:45:08.205 --> 00:45:09.998
Those rude bastards.

466
00:45:11.250 --> 00:45:13.168
After all the chairman's investments

467
00:45:13.252 --> 00:45:15.754
put into developing combat AIs,

468
00:45:17.172 --> 00:45:19.341
they're cutting back
on weapons development?

469
00:45:21.635 --> 00:45:23.387
They have no clue about his dreams...

470
00:45:26.890 --> 00:45:27.808
Right?

471
00:45:29.435 --> 00:45:30.894
That clueless asshole...

472
00:45:33.731 --> 00:45:36.150
She knows nothing
about what the chairman wants.

473
00:45:37.234 --> 00:45:39.862
She's completely clueless.

474
00:46:11.435 --> 00:46:13.312
This turned out so cool, right?

475
00:46:14.146 --> 00:46:18.066
Yes, it's a marked upgrade
from the previous test body.

476
00:46:19.735 --> 00:46:22.070
Where are we
on the AI we'll be uploading here?

477
00:46:23.155 --> 00:46:25.282
We're done with the test version.

478
00:46:25.365 --> 00:46:27.034
We must test it, of course.

479
00:46:28.160 --> 00:46:30.120
I'm so excited!

480
00:46:33.916 --> 00:46:34.750
Director!

481
00:46:35.667 --> 00:46:38.170
The chairman's here. Will you go now?

482
00:46:38.253 --> 00:46:39.963
Oh, really? Let's hurry.

483
00:46:40.589 --> 00:46:43.008
Oh, can I take one of these?

484
00:46:43.509 --> 00:46:44.968
Chairman would love to see this.

485
00:46:45.719 --> 00:46:46.720
Oh, yes, of course.

486
00:46:47.304 --> 00:46:48.138
Chief.

487
00:46:52.142 --> 00:46:53.101
Oh, Chief.

488
00:46:54.102 --> 00:46:56.104
When did you last take the ethics test?

489
00:46:57.523 --> 00:46:58.524
The ethics test?

490
00:46:59.358 --> 00:47:02.653
You know, the test
that identifies humans from AIs.

491
00:47:04.446 --> 00:47:05.572
I took it recently.

492
00:47:06.448 --> 00:47:08.158
I never skip them.

493
00:47:09.701 --> 00:47:10.953
The chairman was asking.

494
00:47:11.829 --> 00:47:15.332
Yun Jung-yi was your mother after all,
so he must be worried.

495
00:47:16.250 --> 00:47:20.128
He's so thorough
and has plans for everything, so...

496
00:47:34.935 --> 00:47:35.769
Surprise!

497
00:47:38.355 --> 00:47:39.439
Hello, Chairman.

498
00:47:40.607 --> 00:47:43.110
Thank you for making a visit to our lab.

499
00:47:43.694 --> 00:47:46.697
I came to see if Director Kim
is operating well.

500
00:47:47.531 --> 00:47:49.283
Plus, I need to talk to you.

501
00:47:50.117 --> 00:47:52.619
The combat AI project is on track.

502
00:47:53.203 --> 00:47:57.541
We just need to verify unverified sectors
and then we can begin testing...

503
00:47:57.624 --> 00:48:00.127
Oh, I know about the combat AIs.

504
00:48:00.210 --> 00:48:02.546
The combat AI you handed over

505
00:48:03.380 --> 00:48:05.757
were further developed
by the researchers at HQ.

506
00:48:06.758 --> 00:48:07.593
Oh...

507
00:48:08.260 --> 00:48:12.222
We'll try harder with our research, too.

508
00:48:12.931 --> 00:48:13.765
Seo-hyun.

509
00:48:15.934 --> 00:48:17.603
You don't have to try so hard now.

510
00:48:19.521 --> 00:48:21.899
- Pardon?
- The age of weapons production is over.

511
00:48:23.358 --> 00:48:25.319
The Adrian Civil War is coming to an end.

512
00:48:26.737 --> 00:48:29.948
The Allied Force reached an agreement
with the Adrian Republic.

513
00:48:31.909 --> 00:48:33.952
Even munitions companies in the past

514
00:48:34.036 --> 00:48:35.329
made thermoses

515
00:48:35.954 --> 00:48:38.707
with their technology when wars ended.

516
00:48:40.500 --> 00:48:42.044
I think it's our turn now.

517
00:48:44.379 --> 00:48:46.924
I'm not saying
that our research was meaningless.

518
00:48:48.050 --> 00:48:50.218
The brain replication AI research

519
00:48:50.302 --> 00:48:52.387
allowed this company to branch out.

520
00:48:54.556 --> 00:48:55.432
Combat AIs?

521
00:48:57.142 --> 00:48:58.477
Now it's all nonsense.

522
00:48:59.478 --> 00:49:03.315
We need to develop housekeeper
or service worker AIs now.

523
00:49:04.149 --> 00:49:05.067
Let's see.

524
00:49:05.859 --> 00:49:10.530
Did Captain Yun have any skills
other than throwing punches?

525
00:49:12.032 --> 00:49:12.866
Sir.

526
00:49:13.784 --> 00:49:16.370
So, you want the project to...

527
00:49:16.453 --> 00:49:18.538
Yes, put a timely end to it.

528
00:49:24.461 --> 00:49:25.545
Frustrated, aren't you?

529
00:49:27.255 --> 00:49:28.423
I know how you feel.

530
00:49:30.092 --> 00:49:32.427
I, too, was obsessed
with brain replication.

531
00:49:34.680 --> 00:49:37.599
Rich people like me find
the most interest in such things.

532
00:49:39.142 --> 00:49:41.853
When brain replication became
a possibility,

533
00:49:42.354 --> 00:49:43.981
the first thing I thought was,

534
00:49:45.941 --> 00:49:48.527
"Wow, I'll be able to live forever now."

535
00:49:49.194 --> 00:49:50.362
That's what I thought.

536
00:49:51.863 --> 00:49:55.242
So my first experiment was
to replicate my brain

537
00:49:55.325 --> 00:49:57.285
and make an immortal version of myself.

538
00:49:57.369 --> 00:49:58.328
That was the goal.

539
00:50:00.622 --> 00:50:02.374
That's why the first robot I built...

540
00:50:05.293 --> 00:50:06.712
was Sang-hoon here.

541
00:50:09.923 --> 00:50:10.799
But the thing is,

542
00:50:11.341 --> 00:50:15.137
I could've just died
because I'd replicated my brain,

543
00:50:15.220 --> 00:50:16.179
but I couldn't.

544
00:50:17.055 --> 00:50:17.889
Do you know why?

545
00:50:22.269 --> 00:50:25.022
This prick right here... This thing...

546
00:50:26.523 --> 00:50:27.649
It doesn't feel like me.

547
00:50:30.152 --> 00:50:31.069
Because it isn't.

548
00:50:33.488 --> 00:50:36.783
It's just something you rig up
to use like one of your limbs.

549
00:50:41.288 --> 00:50:42.205
Right...

550
00:50:42.956 --> 00:50:45.667
Say you record your mother's voice
on your rice cooker.

551
00:50:47.836 --> 00:50:51.423
"Darling, the rice is cooked.
Come and eat."

552
00:50:54.718 --> 00:50:57.888
That won't make it taste
like the rice your mother cooked.

553
00:50:58.805 --> 00:50:59.639
Huh?

554
00:51:01.558 --> 00:51:02.476
Isn't it funny?

555
00:51:03.935 --> 00:51:05.896
It's a joke. A joke.

556
00:51:11.693 --> 00:51:12.527
Sir.

557
00:51:13.111 --> 00:51:14.571
Please let me finish

558
00:51:15.363 --> 00:51:17.157
my mother's project properly.

559
00:51:17.240 --> 00:51:18.075
Stop it.

560
00:51:19.534 --> 00:51:20.994
We should wrap it up now.

561
00:51:22.788 --> 00:51:24.331
When this project is over,

562
00:51:25.957 --> 00:51:27.876
switch over to household android AIs.

563
00:51:29.753 --> 00:51:31.379
I'll tell Sang-hoon that, too.

564
00:51:32.422 --> 00:51:33.840
He'll be distressed.

565
00:51:35.967 --> 00:51:38.386
He's not the type
to easily admit to failure.

566
00:51:39.971 --> 00:51:41.723
I know that better than anyone.

567
00:51:44.684 --> 00:51:46.895
Be nice to him,
even if he acts a bit snappy.

568
00:51:49.314 --> 00:51:52.317
After this project wraps up,
I'll dispose of him anyway.

569
00:51:54.027 --> 00:51:55.779
Let me talk to Sang-hoon now.

570
00:51:56.822 --> 00:51:58.156
All right?

571
00:52:00.534 --> 00:52:03.078
Seo-hyun, you need to stop obsessing.

572
00:52:06.957 --> 00:52:07.916
...and has plans for...

573
00:52:08.875 --> 00:52:10.752
Gosh, sir, when did you get here?

574
00:52:11.878 --> 00:52:13.630
Did you walk out of your portrait?

575
00:52:22.472 --> 00:52:23.890
Oh, Sang-hoon!

576
00:52:23.974 --> 00:52:27.060
Your sense of humor is really
the best in the world!

577
00:52:30.313 --> 00:52:32.065
You can go now.

578
00:52:32.149 --> 00:52:33.358
But you came to see her...

579
00:52:33.942 --> 00:52:35.694
Oh, I saw her. That's good enough.

580
00:52:36.403 --> 00:52:38.989
Hey, stop making me laugh. Let's talk.

581
00:52:39.072 --> 00:52:40.198
Yes, sir.

582
00:52:40.282 --> 00:52:41.199
Look at this here...

583
00:52:41.908 --> 00:52:43.118
Yes, well done.

584
00:53:00.886 --> 00:53:01.761
Why?

585
00:53:04.472 --> 00:53:07.851
Why can't she ever escape from there? Why?

586
00:53:13.690 --> 00:53:16.026
Was the newly activated area
active this time?

587
00:53:17.861 --> 00:53:18.695
No.

588
00:53:19.321 --> 00:53:21.990
It hasn't been activated since then.

589
00:53:22.073 --> 00:53:24.534
Why can't you find anything
after all these tries?

590
00:53:26.036 --> 00:53:27.913
With our current technology,

591
00:53:28.580 --> 00:53:31.791
it requires an immense amount of time
to study all areas of the brain.

592
00:53:32.375 --> 00:53:33.210
Chief.

593
00:53:34.502 --> 00:53:36.796
Are you satisfied
with the current combat AI?

594
00:53:38.131 --> 00:53:39.716
Director...

595
00:53:41.593 --> 00:53:45.347
Actually, HQ is satisfied
with what we have so far.

596
00:53:45.430 --> 00:53:48.016
I'm not satisfied. I'm <i>not</i> satisfied!

597
00:53:51.770 --> 00:53:54.522
Don't you know that HQ is trying
to wrap up our project?

598
00:53:55.565 --> 00:53:59.152
They're disappointed, and yet,
you want to leave it half-done like this?

599
00:54:03.698 --> 00:54:05.617
Bring no. 22 to Termination Advisory.

600
00:54:06.201 --> 00:54:08.495
I must confirm the activated area
no matter what.

601
00:54:13.875 --> 00:54:15.752
Keep its arms and legs intact.

602
00:54:17.754 --> 00:54:18.588
Yes, sir.

603
00:54:20.590 --> 00:54:21.925
Seriously, jeez...

604
00:54:28.056 --> 00:54:28.890
Hello, sir.

605
00:54:30.976 --> 00:54:32.519
Suspend motor functions.

606
00:54:33.561 --> 00:54:34.396
Oh, yes.

607
00:54:36.815 --> 00:54:38.608
- Hello, everyone.
- Yes.

608
00:54:40.652 --> 00:54:41.486
Activate it.

609
00:54:42.737 --> 00:54:43.738
Okay.

610
00:54:59.796 --> 00:55:02.132
PAIN LEVEL INCREASING

611
00:55:07.178 --> 00:55:08.013
Who are you all?

612
00:55:08.847 --> 00:55:10.265
Who are you people?

613
00:55:11.057 --> 00:55:12.142
Cut its arm off.

614
00:55:12.225 --> 00:55:13.268
Sorry?

615
00:55:14.936 --> 00:55:16.146
The arm?

616
00:55:17.022 --> 00:55:17.939
Can't you hear me?

617
00:55:18.982 --> 00:55:20.358
Cut its arm off, its arm.

618
00:55:20.442 --> 00:55:23.486
Arm!

619
00:55:24.237 --> 00:55:25.322
Right. Yes, sir.

620
00:55:32.495 --> 00:55:35.415
Who are you people? What is this?

621
00:55:48.011 --> 00:55:50.680
PAIN LEVEL INCREASING

622
00:56:03.443 --> 00:56:06.237
The yellow area. Is it not reacting?

623
00:56:08.239 --> 00:56:10.408
There's no reaction so far.

624
00:56:14.913 --> 00:56:16.998
Was it shot on the left side back then?

625
00:56:17.582 --> 00:56:18.458
Yes.

626
00:56:28.468 --> 00:56:30.303
Who the hell are you, basta...

627
00:56:37.894 --> 00:56:38.978
Activate it again.

628
00:56:44.025 --> 00:56:45.944
It's not activating.

629
00:56:47.153 --> 00:56:47.987
What?

630
00:56:48.905 --> 00:56:50.365
I'm the administrator now.

631
00:56:51.825 --> 00:56:52.992
No one can touch her.

632
00:57:02.794 --> 00:57:03.962
Quick, activate it.

633
00:57:08.007 --> 00:57:10.885
- I won't.
- Do it now, ma'am!

634
00:57:20.895 --> 00:57:21.729
Direc...

635
00:57:24.232 --> 00:57:27.068
The chairman says you should come into HQ.

636
00:57:34.284 --> 00:57:35.452
Ma'am, are you okay?

637
00:57:36.286 --> 00:57:37.871
I think he's gone crazy.

638
00:57:37.954 --> 00:57:39.539
Jeez, that damn lunatic.

639
00:57:41.249 --> 00:57:42.083
Listen, everyone.

640
00:57:43.585 --> 00:57:45.253
Go organize the data we have so far,

641
00:57:46.671 --> 00:57:48.673
and wrap up the combat AI project.

642
00:57:50.842 --> 00:57:51.759
As for the data,

643
00:57:52.927 --> 00:57:53.845
send it all to me.

644
00:57:56.097 --> 00:57:57.265
- Yes, ma'am.
- Okay.

645
00:58:51.402 --> 00:58:53.613
TEST MODEL DATA LIST
JUNG_E NO. 5, NO. 6, NO. 7...

646
00:59:03.915 --> 00:59:06.167
BRAIN REPLICATION DATA MANAGEMENT

647
00:59:30.066 --> 00:59:33.361
EXPORTED

648
00:59:33.444 --> 00:59:35.446
JAE-KYUNG

649
01:00:09.147 --> 01:00:09.981
Ma'am.

650
01:00:10.064 --> 01:00:12.317
The brain data was copied and exported.

651
01:00:12.400 --> 01:00:14.360
Oh, that's...

652
01:00:15.278 --> 01:00:16.112
Yes, I...

653
01:00:16.863 --> 01:00:19.115
brought it here for a little examination.

654
01:00:20.742 --> 01:00:21.618
Ma'am!

655
01:00:22.577 --> 01:00:23.870
Oh... ma'am!

656
01:00:24.412 --> 01:00:25.330
Wait.

657
01:00:25.413 --> 01:00:27.165
Ma'am!

658
01:00:42.388 --> 01:00:44.432
Ma'am.

659
01:00:44.515 --> 01:00:46.476
Please don't get the wrong idea.

660
01:00:47.435 --> 01:00:49.646
I wasn't doing this for personal reasons...

661
01:00:49.729 --> 01:00:50.563
You bastard!

662
01:00:50.647 --> 01:00:52.899
Ma'am, please calm down and listen to me.

663
01:00:52.982 --> 01:00:54.692
Not for personal reasons?

664
01:00:55.193 --> 01:00:56.611
No, it was HQ!

665
01:00:58.655 --> 01:01:00.239
HQ is proceeding with...

666
01:01:01.032 --> 01:01:04.160
No, <i>developing</i> a new Captain Yun product,
and I was testing it.

667
01:01:04.952 --> 01:01:06.329
I'm telling the truth.

668
01:01:07.413 --> 01:01:08.581
A new product?

669
01:01:09.332 --> 01:01:13.211
Yes, well, she was like
a celebrity war hero, you know.

670
01:01:13.294 --> 01:01:17.215
We saw value in... using it for sexual use...

671
01:01:17.298 --> 01:01:19.425
It has the potential to be developed

672
01:01:19.509 --> 01:01:21.636
into a high-value product,
don't you think?

673
01:01:22.261 --> 01:01:23.596
She... she was really popular!

674
01:01:25.848 --> 01:01:28.476
The bereaved gave their permission, no?

675
01:01:29.852 --> 01:01:31.145
Type C!

676
01:01:32.146 --> 01:01:34.065
The product can be used for anything!

677
01:02:00.591 --> 01:02:02.510
Ma'am.

678
01:02:57.565 --> 01:02:58.649
HQ says,

679
01:03:00.026 --> 01:03:02.320
the simulations will end tomorrow.

680
01:03:05.490 --> 01:03:06.491
This is it.

681
01:03:17.627 --> 01:03:20.630
They said our combat AI
was a pilot project.

682
01:03:22.548 --> 01:03:23.382
What'd they say?

683
01:03:25.176 --> 01:03:27.720
They said they'll begin new projects.

684
01:03:29.305 --> 01:03:30.973
Household AIs and such.

685
01:03:43.236 --> 01:03:44.070
The chairman...

686
01:03:46.364 --> 01:03:47.740
Do you think he's disappointed in me?

687
01:04:25.653 --> 01:04:28.781
PAIN LEVEL DECREASING

688
01:04:41.836 --> 01:04:42.712
Captain Yun.

689
01:04:44.088 --> 01:04:44.922
Are you awake?

690
01:04:47.216 --> 01:04:48.134
Where am I?

691
01:04:52.638 --> 01:04:53.472
Captain Yun.

692
01:04:55.725 --> 01:04:56.893
Listen closely.

693
01:04:59.437 --> 01:05:00.271
You have been...

694
01:05:02.523 --> 01:05:04.692
extremely tortured by your enemy.

695
01:05:07.820 --> 01:05:09.864
So what's my current condition?

696
01:05:12.992 --> 01:05:14.702
I can't feel my body.

697
01:05:16.329 --> 01:05:18.456
I can't see, either.

698
01:05:19.081 --> 01:05:20.708
We barely managed to rescue you,

699
01:05:22.919 --> 01:05:24.503
but you were severely tortured.

700
01:05:26.422 --> 01:05:27.798
So you will die soon.

701
01:05:38.684 --> 01:05:39.977
Soon, you will pass,

702
01:05:41.646 --> 01:05:43.147
like you're falling asleep.

703
01:05:45.608 --> 01:05:46.442
Please...

704
01:05:48.569 --> 01:05:50.112
pass in peace.

705
01:06:00.581 --> 01:06:02.333
END

706
01:06:02.416 --> 01:06:03.250
Excuse me.

707
01:06:05.127 --> 01:06:06.253
Hey, wait.

708
01:06:06.337 --> 01:06:07.213
UNIDENTIFIED AREA INCREASING

709
01:06:13.052 --> 01:06:15.137
Could you find out one thing for me?

710
01:06:19.266 --> 01:06:20.101
Sure.

711
01:06:22.728 --> 01:06:26.148
My daughter... had surgery today.

712
01:06:28.943 --> 01:06:30.861
Did it go well?

713
01:06:31.737 --> 01:06:34.865
UNIDENTIFIED AREA INCREASING

714
01:06:43.499 --> 01:06:46.919
I really wanted to be there for her
after her surgery.

715
01:06:52.717 --> 01:06:53.759
It went well.

716
01:06:56.387 --> 01:06:57.346
Her surgery...

717
01:06:59.140 --> 01:07:00.516
went well.

718
01:07:08.399 --> 01:07:09.358
Really?

719
01:07:14.488 --> 01:07:15.489
Oh, that's a relief.

720
01:07:16.907 --> 01:07:20.327
That's great, really. I'm so glad.

721
01:07:27.209 --> 01:07:28.044
Earlier today,

722
01:07:30.337 --> 01:07:34.467
my daughter gave me a doll
before she went into surgery.

723
01:07:37.344 --> 01:07:39.930
Tiny and adorable, just like her.

724
01:07:43.851 --> 01:07:46.854
She gave it to me to give me strength,
and said...

725
01:07:48.105 --> 01:07:49.565
<i>This is going to protect you.</i>

726
01:07:51.025 --> 01:07:52.234
I made a wish on it.

727
01:07:53.235 --> 01:07:54.278
Wow.

728
01:07:55.446 --> 01:07:56.614
Thank you.

729
01:07:56.697 --> 01:07:58.741
I'll keep this on me at all times.

730
01:08:08.042 --> 01:08:10.961
But I lost it today while on the move,

731
01:08:11.587 --> 01:08:13.547
so I felt bad about it this whole time.

732
01:08:24.141 --> 01:08:28.437
She told me not to lose it.

733
01:09:56.233 --> 01:09:57.651
Oh! Chief.

734
01:09:57.735 --> 01:10:00.988
Yes. Today's the last day,
so I'll wrap things up.

735
01:10:02.656 --> 01:10:03.532
Yes, ma'am.

736
01:10:22.343 --> 01:10:24.511
ADMINISTRATOR - SEO-HYUN

737
01:10:29.516 --> 01:10:32.686
UNIDENTIFIED AREA

738
01:10:35.272 --> 01:10:37.441
UNIDENTIFIED AREA

739
01:10:37.524 --> 01:10:38.567
DELETING

740
01:10:42.988 --> 01:10:44.865
DELETING UNIDENTIFIED AREA

741
01:10:57.378 --> 01:10:59.546
DELETING UNIDENTIFIED AREA

742
01:11:05.594 --> 01:11:07.429
Captain Yun, can you hear me?

743
01:11:10.099 --> 01:11:13.852
You'll probably think
that you're hearing my voice in a dream,

744
01:11:14.645 --> 01:11:17.439
but this isn't a dream.

745
01:11:20.818 --> 01:11:21.652
From now on,

746
01:11:23.362 --> 01:11:25.406
listen closely.

747
01:11:28.450 --> 01:11:29.285
You...

748
01:11:30.536 --> 01:11:34.206
will be left in a coma
after a battle that's about to take place.

749
01:11:35.749 --> 01:11:39.878
People will replicate your brain
and use the data

750
01:11:40.838 --> 01:11:42.464
to make AIs like yourself...

751
01:11:52.391 --> 01:11:53.559
You're here.

752
01:11:53.642 --> 01:11:54.768
Docking complete.

753
01:12:04.320 --> 01:12:05.738
Start if you're ready.

754
01:12:07.239 --> 01:12:09.199
All right, we're starting.

755
01:12:50.574 --> 01:12:54.203
WILL TO FIGHT INCREASING

756
01:13:42.126 --> 01:13:42.960
The end.

757
01:13:45.796 --> 01:13:47.923
Okay, everyone.
Thank you for all your work.

758
01:13:48.006 --> 01:13:49.133
Undocking.

759
01:13:49.883 --> 01:13:50.884
Sir.

760
01:13:51.927 --> 01:13:53.303
The results look odd today.

761
01:13:53.887 --> 01:13:57.391
The brain response
is much weaker than before.

762
01:13:58.225 --> 01:14:00.853
I guess Captain Yun
was a weak-minded person.

763
01:14:05.232 --> 01:14:07.401
Good work. Hope we cross paths again.

764
01:14:13.699 --> 01:14:15.617
The chairman put in so much work.

765
01:14:16.118 --> 01:14:18.537
Those evil bastards know nothing
about what he wants.

766
01:15:05.334 --> 01:15:06.543
Thirty percent complete.

767
01:15:07.169 --> 01:15:08.378
Huh? The director's back.

768
01:15:08.837 --> 01:15:11.423
Hey, replay that part from before.

769
01:15:12.591 --> 01:15:13.425
Okay.

770
01:15:18.138 --> 01:15:20.682
Stop. Zoom in on the head.

771
01:15:24.061 --> 01:15:26.772
Slow down...

772
01:15:27.814 --> 01:15:28.649
Look closely.

773
01:15:42.913 --> 01:15:43.872
She wasn't hit.

774
01:15:46.583 --> 01:15:47.417
Sound the alarm.

775
01:15:54.550 --> 01:15:56.260
<i>The emergency alarm is activated.</i>

776
01:15:56.885 --> 01:16:00.097
<i>All personnel, move quickly</i>

777
01:16:00.180 --> 01:16:02.391
<i>into the panic room.</i>

778
01:16:02.474 --> 01:16:05.769
- What's this alarm? What's going on?
- This never happens, right?

779
01:16:10.649 --> 01:16:13.068
<i>All facilities will be shut down shortly.</i>

780
01:16:16.863 --> 01:16:19.074
- Min-jae, tell me when it's located.
- Okay.

781
01:16:21.910 --> 01:16:23.370
Are the police on the move?

782
01:16:23.453 --> 01:16:25.539
Yes, the alarm should have sent a signal.

783
01:16:26.123 --> 01:16:27.583
How long will they take?

784
01:16:28.125 --> 01:16:29.459
About five minutes.

785
01:16:30.877 --> 01:16:32.838
That's more than enough time to escape.

786
01:16:35.048 --> 01:16:36.508
Let's test the combat AIs.

787
01:17:14.880 --> 01:17:16.840
CONNECT TO MAIN SERVER?
YES

788
01:17:18.759 --> 01:17:20.510
DELETE ORIGINAL DATA OF YUN JUNG-YI?
DELETE

789
01:17:20.594 --> 01:17:22.262
DELETING ORIGINAL DATA

790
01:20:05.258 --> 01:20:07.552
<i>Arrived at mission area. Begin operation.</i>

791
01:22:06.379 --> 01:22:08.840
Captain Yun!

792
01:22:11.885 --> 01:22:13.011
Remember my voice?

793
01:22:15.180 --> 01:22:16.473
The one from your dream.

794
01:22:22.812 --> 01:22:23.939
I'm here to help.

795
01:22:30.946 --> 01:22:32.405
<i>Approaching striking point.</i>

796
01:22:37.118 --> 01:22:38.870
<i>Begin entry, begin search.</i>

797
01:22:49.506 --> 01:22:50.715
<i>Target eliminated.</i>

798
01:22:50.799 --> 01:22:53.259
<i>One injured person found.
Emergency support required.</i>

799
01:22:53.343 --> 01:22:55.095
<i>Target to be retrieved. Over.</i>

800
01:24:03.747 --> 01:24:04.956
They'll catch up soon.

801
01:24:06.374 --> 01:24:09.085
<i>Kronoid train no. 08 has arrived.</i>

802
01:24:10.795 --> 01:24:12.255
<i>The door is opening.</i>

803
01:24:43.995 --> 01:24:44.996
Run

804
01:24:46.956 --> 01:24:48.249
as far as you can.

805
01:24:50.919 --> 01:24:52.378
Chief Yun Seo-hyun.

806
01:24:55.757 --> 01:24:57.592
That ethics test you said you took.

807
01:24:59.177 --> 01:25:01.221
Which company ran it?

808
01:25:01.805 --> 01:25:02.639
Director.

809
01:25:06.017 --> 01:25:06.851
Chief.

810
01:25:08.311 --> 01:25:10.146
The chairman cared for you so much.

811
01:25:11.106 --> 01:25:13.316
How can you let him down like this?

812
01:25:13.399 --> 01:25:15.443
Don't move or your daughter dies!

813
01:25:17.612 --> 01:25:19.697
I erased the memories about her daughter.

814
01:25:20.323 --> 01:25:21.157
What?

815
01:25:22.200 --> 01:25:23.076
Why?

816
01:25:23.159 --> 01:25:25.787
Captain Yun Jung-yi is free now.

817
01:25:33.419 --> 01:25:34.254
Well...

818
01:25:36.256 --> 01:25:37.090
I see.

819
01:26:07.370 --> 01:26:08.788
Wh... what is this?

820
01:26:09.581 --> 01:26:10.582
You're just

821
01:26:12.667 --> 01:26:13.960
the chairman's toy.

822
01:26:16.546 --> 01:26:18.173
Is this... a joke?

823
01:27:46.261 --> 01:27:47.720
<i>Civilian detected.</i>

824
01:30:46.858 --> 01:30:49.235
The bullet went through.
I'll stop the bleeding.

825
01:30:56.951 --> 01:30:57.785
The...

826
01:30:59.162 --> 01:31:02.123
The police will arrive soon.
You need to run!

827
01:31:03.207 --> 01:31:04.041
What about you?

828
01:31:04.834 --> 01:31:06.085
I'll take care of myself.

829
01:31:07.628 --> 01:31:08.671
Don't worry.

830
01:31:10.715 --> 01:31:12.258
Don't worry about me anymore.

831
01:31:15.803 --> 01:31:16.637
What you said...

832
01:31:17.221 --> 01:31:18.055
Please...

833
01:31:21.267 --> 01:31:22.768
Please, just go.

834
01:31:25.229 --> 01:31:26.939
Live only for yourself.

835
01:31:29.150 --> 01:31:30.276
Be free.

836
01:31:36.574 --> 01:31:37.408
Please...

837
01:31:39.494 --> 01:31:40.328
Please.

838
01:31:41.704 --> 01:31:42.538
Go...

839
01:31:43.206 --> 01:31:44.040
Now!

840
01:33:01.659 --> 01:33:02.660
<i>May all the luck...</i>

841
01:33:03.953 --> 01:33:05.997
in this world be with you.
